    <briefdescription>
<para>Stores the pre-edit snapshots of transactions on disk, so that <computeroutput>saw undo</computeroutput> can restore them. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each transaction has one record file and one blob file per original file. The record file holds the JSON of the transaction. A blob file holds the bytes of one original file.</para>
<para>A record is staged in the pending folder, published with one rename into the undo folder, and claimed by <computeroutput>undo</computeroutput> with the reverse rename. No lock exists. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
